(The economic period is the UTC interval between 00:00 and 00:00 the next day. The cutoff ends) Tj T*
(result collection, but payments are linked to the original round regardless of the current) Tj T*
(period.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Approved policies must set execution windows, deadlines, and sources. Without validated) Tj T*
(parameters, distribution is not authorized. Closure occurs upon the end of the window or) Tj T*
(completion of payments.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Weights are calculated post-cutoff on eligible balances. Entries await the next round; exits) Tj T*
(nullify weights. Post-cutoff exits cancel pending rights without altering results of new) Tj T*
(rounds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Settlement decisions fix beneficiaries and weights, considering confirmed exits. Subsequent) Tj T*
(exits cancel credits without redistribution or new splits. Historical records and current) Tj T*
(weights are distinct.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Calculation and execution are part of the current round. Financial closure eliminates unsent) Tj T*
(rights; ongoing payments remain in reconciliation. There is no reopening or post-closure) Tj T*
(credit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Payment plans follow deterministic order and use atomic execution when validated for the) Tj T*
(network. If there is partial processing, they publish who received, who did not, and the cause;) Tj T*
(failures may cause definitive loss of unsent portions at closing, and that risk must be) Tj T*
(disclosed in advance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(BETTEX exit and payment order) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Network order prevails over backend messages. BETTEX exits before USDC receipt cancel rights.) Tj T*
(Equal timestamps or insufficient evidence suspend finalization.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Bank reserves do not prevent external transfers. Eligibility requires on-network validation) Tj T*
(with sortable events. Isolated off-chain checks do not guarantee automatic payment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Canceling rights does not reverse transfers or prove USDC recovery. Reconciliations with) Tj T*
(improper receipt generate treasury losses without charging the participant or restoring) Tj T*
(credits.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Settlement costs and temporal origin) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Costs belong to the period of occurrence, not the payment round. Round and economic period) Tj T*
(records must be distinct to avoid double counting.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Before authorizing the split, reserve principal and the cost cap for each asset and project) Tj T*
(liquidity after all disbursements. A cost reserve is not an incurred expense. Identify its) Tj T*
(source and authorization; do not silently deduct costs from the participant’s right or the) Tj T*
(exclusive repurchase portion. Reconcile differences between reserved and actual cost; surplus) Tj T*
(is not new profit. Without sufficient budget and coverage, do not authorize the split.) Tj T*
